  "generated_text": "To determine the number of possible pairings of a bowl and a glass, we need to consider the number of choices available for each item and then multiply these choices together.\n\n1. **Identify the number of choices for the bowl:**\n   Chandra has 4 bowls, each of a different color (red, blue, yellow, green).\n   - Therefore, there are 4 choices for the bowl.\n\n2. **Identify the number of choices for the glass:**\n   Chandra has exactly one glass of the same color as each bowl.\n   - Therefore, there are 4 choices for the glass.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of pairings:**\n   - For each choice of the bowl, there are 4 possible choices for the glass.\n   - Thus, the total number of pairings is the product of the number of choices for the bowl and the number of choices for the glass.\n   - This is calculated as:\n     \\[\n     4 \\text{ bowl choices} \\times 4 \\text{ glass choices} = 16 \\text{ pairings}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of possible pairings is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).",
